 * @li @ref xpost_intro
 * @li @ref xpost_design
 *
 * @section xpost_intro Introduction
 *
 * xpost is a PostScript LanguageLevel 3 interpreter, built as a shared
 * library (libxpost) with a command-line interpreter and an embedding
 * example on top of it. README.md at the tree root describes what it
 * implements, its output devices, and how it is tested; doc/COMPAT
 * records the deviations from the published language.
 *
 * @section xpost_compilation Compilation and installation
 *
 * The primary build is meson:
 *
 * @verbatim
meson setup builddir
meson compile -C builddir
meson install -C builddir
   @endverbatim
 *
 * The tree also carries an autotools build (./autogen.sh, ./configure,
 * make, make install), which builds the same programs. README.md
 * documents both, and the internals are described in doc/INTERNALS and
 * its companions.
 *
 * This reference is generated by doxygen from the library and program
 * sources; the make target is @c doc under autotools, and the @c doc
 * custom target under meson.
 */
